      "description": "Plaque for the anchor from the wreck of the Rydal Hall, in Pillar Point Harbor, California. The text says:\nANCHOR OF THE RYDAL HALL \nOn the night of October 17, 1876, \nthe square-rigger Rydal Hall, en \nroute from Cardiff, Wales, to \nSan Francisco with a cargo of \ncoal, ran on the rocks in a heavy \nfog off Pillar Point and was lost. \nNinety-five years later this \nanchor, fourteen feet long and \nweighing two tons, was recovered \nfrom the sea[,] a reminder of more \nthan 85 sailing ships wrecked on \nthe San Mateo County coastside in \nthe last half of the nineteenth  \ncentury.\n\n.",
